---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  titulo="Cookie Policy | Doria Clinic"
  descripcion="Which cookies the Doria Clinic website uses: technical hosting cookies and third-party cookies from the embedded Google map."
  h1="Cookie policy"
  anchoCompleto
>
  <h2>What cookies are</h2>
  <p>
    Cookies are small files that a website installs on your browser, allowing it,
    among other things, to store and retrieve information about your browsing
    habits.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies used on this website</h2>
  <p>
    This is a static website: it has no analytics system of its own and no
    advertising cookies. The only cookies that may be installed are:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Cloudflare technical cookies</strong>, from our hosting provider,
      necessary to serve the website securely and to balance load between
      servers. They are not used for advertising purposes.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Google Maps cookies</strong>: on the site's pages we embed a Google
      map to show the clinic's location. When you interact with the map, Google
      may set its own cookies, subject to{' '}
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        Google's privacy policy
      </a>.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    None of this website's contact buttons (WhatsApp, call, email) install
    cookies: they simply open the corresponding app on your device.
  </p>

  <h2>How to disable cookies</h2>
  <p>
    You can allow, block or delete cookies installed on your device through your
    browser's settings. Please note that blocking Google Maps cookies may prevent
    the map from displaying correctly.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We will update this page if we introduce analytics tools or other services
    that use cookies in the future.
  </p>

  <p><em>Last updated: September 2026.</em></p>
</Base>
